"␛[1mpyreon-lint --list␛[22m ␛[38;2;138;134;150m· 134 rules in 10 groups␛[39m

  ␛[1mPYREON␛[22m ␛[38;2;138;134;150m(54) — framework semantics — nothing outside Pyreon can know these␛[39m
    pyreon/no-async-effect  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow async functions in \`effect()\` / \`renderEffect()\` / \`computed()\` — signal reads after
      the first await are not tracked.
    pyreon/no-bare-signal-in-jsx  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      STYLE-ONLY: prefer the explicit \`{() => sig()}\` accessor form over bare \`{sig()}\` in JSX text.
      NOT a correctness rule — the compiler lowers BOTH forms to the SAME reactive \`_bindText(sig,
      node)\` binding, so bare \`{sig()}\` is already fully reactive. Opt-in.
    pyreon/no-context-destructure  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Disallow destructuring useContext() — it breaks reactivity when context provides getters.
    pyreon/no-signal-in-loop  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow creating signals or computeds inside loops.
    pyreon/no-signal-in-props  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Signal call in component prop — value captured once unless compiler wraps it. Use props.x
      pattern for reactivity.
    pyreon/no-nested-effect  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn against nesting effect() inside another effect().
    pyreon/no-peek-in-tracked  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow .peek() inside effect() or computed() — it bypasses tracking.
    pyreon/no-unbatched-updates  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when 3+ .set() calls can fire on the SAME execution path in a function without batch().
    pyreon/prefer-computed  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Suggest computed() when an effect only contains a single .set() call.
    pyreon/no-effect-assignment  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when an effect only contains a single .update() call.
    pyreon/no-signal-leak  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn about unused signal declarations (potential leaks).
    pyreon/no-signal-call-write  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow \`sig(value)\` write attempts on signal/computed bindings — \`signal()\` is the read-only
      callable. Use \`sig.set(value)\` or \`sig.update(fn)\`. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/storage-signal-v-forwarding  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Signal-wrapper callables delegating \`.direct\` to a base signal must also forward the internal
      \`_v\` field. Without forwarding, the compiler-emitted \`_bindText\` fast path reads \`undefined\`
      and renders empty text post-hydration.
    pyreon/no-iterate-children-without-resolve  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Library code that iterates \`props.children\` at the VNode level (\`cloneVNode(children, …)\`,
      \`(Array.isArray(children) ? children : [children]).map/filter(…)\`, or \`children.props\`) must
      first unwrap a possible compiler-emitted accessor function — call \`resolveChildren(…)\` or
      \`typeof X === "function" ? X() : X\` at the body entry. Without it, the Pyreon compiler's
      prop-inlining wrap silently produces \`{type: undefined}\` → \`<undefined>\` DOM tags.
    pyreon/no-guard-only-signal-reads-in-effect  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      Flag effects whose EVERY reactive read sits behind a non-reactive guard — the first run can
      short-circuit before any read, so the effect subscribes to nothing and never re-runs.
    pyreon/plain-mode-footgun  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Report every Plain Mode compile-time warning (shallow-state mutation, write to derived,
      unlowerable signalOf, …) as an error.
    pyreon/no-stale-for-item-field  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      A keyed \`<For>\` row reads a field of its item while this file replaces items under the same
      key — on the web the row keeps the first value (iOS/Android redraw). Read the live value by
      key through a call, or give the field its own signal.
    pyreon/no-map-in-jsx  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Prefer <For> over .map() inside JSX for reactive list rendering.
    pyreon/use-by-not-key  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Use \`by\` prop on <For> instead of \`key\` — JSX reserves \`key\` for VNode reconciliation. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-classname  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Use \`class\` instead of \`className\` — Pyreon uses standard HTML attributes. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-htmlfor  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Use \`for\` instead of \`htmlFor\` — Pyreon uses standard HTML attributes. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-onchange  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Prefer \`onInput\` over \`onChange\` on input elements for keypress-by-keypress updates. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-ternary-conditional  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Style preference for <Show> over a ternary with JSX branches. Opt-in — NOT a correctness or
      efficiency rule: the compiler lowers \`{cond ? <a/> : <b/>}\` and \`<Show>\` to the SAME reactive
      \`_mountSlot(() => …)\` accessor, so they mount, swap, and unmount identically. \`<Show>\` adds
      \`fallback\`/\`keyed\`, but a ternary is fully valid and not measurably slower.
    pyreon/no-and-conditional  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Style preference for <Show> over \`&&\` with JSX. Opt-in — NOT a correctness rule: the compiler
      lowers \`{cond && <el/>}\` and \`<Show>\` to the SAME reactive \`_mountSlot(() => …)\` accessor, so
      they mount, swap, and unmount identically. \`<Show>\` adds \`fallback\`/\`keyed\` and a well-tested
      reactive boundary, but bare \`&&\` is fully valid conditional rendering.
    pyreon/no-line-comment-in-jsx  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      A \`//\` line in JSX child position is not a comment — JSX has no line comments, so it renders
      as literal text on web AND, through PMTC, on iOS and Android. Use \`{/* … */}\`.
    pyreon/no-index-as-by  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Disallow using index as \`by\` prop on <For> — use a unique key instead.
    pyreon/no-missing-for-by  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Require a \`by\` prop on \`<For>\` — without it, keyed reconciliation is defeated and every update
      remounts the whole list.
    pyreon/no-props-destructure  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow destructuring props in component functions — breaks reactive prop tracking. Use
      props.x or splitProps().
    pyreon/no-children-access  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mjsx␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      Inform about direct props.children access in renderer files.
    pyreon/no-missing-cleanup  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when onMount uses setInterval/addEventListener without returning a cleanup function.
    pyreon/no-mount-in-effect  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when onMount is called inside effect().
    pyreon/no-effect-in-mount  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      Inform when effect() is created inside onMount — effects are typically created at setup time.
    pyreon/no-dom-in-setup  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when DOM query methods are used outside onMount or effect.
    pyreon/no-imperative-effect-on-create  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Flag \`effect()\` calls at component body level whose callback does imperative work (DOM access,
      async/IO, addEventListener, setTimeout) — that work belongs in \`onMount\`, not in a
      per-instance reactive effect.
    pyreon/init-fn-needs-idempotency  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mlifecycle␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Flag exported \`init*\` functions called from the same module without a refcount / boolean guard
      — register effects N times if called from N component bodies.
    pyreon/no-effect-in-for  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mperformance␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn when effect() is created inside <For> — creates effects per item on every reconciliation.
    pyreon/no-eager-import  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mperformance␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      Suggest lazy-loading heavy Pyreon packages (charts, code, document, flow).
    pyreon/no-heavy-import-only-in-handler  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mperformance␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      A statically-imported heavy module used only in event handlers / lifecycle callbacks should be
      a dynamic import().
    pyreon/prefer-show-over-display  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mperformance␛[39m  ␛[38;2;34;211;238minfo␛[39m
      Suggest <Show> over a conditional \`display\` style — with the trade-off flagged. Opt-in:
      toggling \`display\` keeps a STABLE SSR tree shape (the element is always mounted), which is
      hydration-safe and ref-safe. \`<Show>\`/\`&&\` compile to a slot marker that SSR omits when falsy,
      changing the tree shape — prefer it only when the node needn’t stay mounted. Neither is
      universally correct, so this is an opt-in hint.
    pyreon/promise-race-needs-cleartimeout  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mperformance␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Flag \`Promise.race([work, setTimeout-reject])\` without a corresponding \`clearTimeout\` in a
      \`finally\` block — the timer leaks until it fires when \`work\` wins the race.
    pyreon/no-window-in-ssr  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssr␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Disallow browser globals outside onMount/effect/typeof guards — they break SSR.
    pyreon/no-mismatch-risk  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssr␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn about non-deterministic calls (Date.now, Math.random, crypto.randomUUID) in JSX context
      that cause hydration mismatches.
    pyreon/prefer-request-context  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssr␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Warn about module-level signal()/createStore() in server files — use request context instead.
    pyreon/prefer-isserver  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssr␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Prefer \`isServer\` / \`isClient\` from \`@pyreon/reactivity\` over hand-rolled \`typeof window\` /
      \`typeof document\` checks — they single-source SSR detection (PR #1503) and use the reliable
      \`typeof document\` discriminator. Recommended-level warn, gated on the project depending on
      @pyreon/reactivity. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-private-env-in-client  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssr␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Flag raw \`process.env.X\` / \`import.meta.env.X\` reads in client-reachable @pyreon/zero code —
      \`process.env\` is undefined in the browser and \`import.meta.env\` is bundler-specific. Use
      \`publicEnv()\` from \`@pyreon/zero/env\` with a \`ZERO_PUBLIC_\`-prefixed var (inlined into the
      client bundle at build, secrets kept out). Opt-in best-practice, gated on the project
      depending on @pyreon/zero; \`NODE_ENV\` + Vite built-ins + server-only files are never flagged.
    pyreon/no-deep-import  ␛[38;2;138;134;150marchitecture␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Disallow importing from @pyreon/*/src/, /dist/, or /lib/ — use public exports instead.
    pyreon/island-import-from-client  ␛[38;2;138;134;150marchitecture␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Import \`island\` from '@pyreon/server/client' (or '@pyreon/zero'), never the '@pyreon/server'
      barrel — the barrel drags node:* + the server singleton into client bundles.
    pyreon/dev-guard-warnings  ␛[38;2;138;134;150marchitecture␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Require console.warn/error calls to be wrapped in a dev-only guard (\`if (process.env.NODE_ENV
      !== "production")\` — the bundler-agnostic form; \`__DEV__\` is also accepted as a
      framework-internal alias) so they tree-shake in production.
    pyreon/no-module-signal-in-server-package  ␛[38;2;138;134;150marchitecture␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Forbid module-scoped Pyreon signals in server-side framework packages. Server packages are
      concurrent — module signals race between requests. Use per-request \`AsyncLocalStorage\` or the
      framework context system instead. See the i18n-routing.ts \`localeSignal\` precedent for the
      canonical fix shape.
    pyreon/no-process-dev-gate  ␛[38;2;138;134;150marchitecture␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      Forbid bundler-coupled dev gates: \`typeof process !== "undefined" && process.env.NODE_ENV !==
      "production"\` is dead in Vite browser bundles, and \`import.meta.env.DEV\` is Vite/Rolldown-only
      (dead in Webpack/Next.js, esbuild, Rollup, Parcel, Bun). Use bundler-agnostic
      \`process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production"\` — every modern bundler auto-replaces it at consumer
      build time. ␛[38;2;74;222;128mfixable␛[39m
    pyreon/no-unguarded-async-signal-write  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mreactivity␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      An async function that writes captured signal state after an \`await\` with no staleness guard —
      a slow earlier response resolves last and clobbers newer data (leak class F).
    pyreon/invalid-loader-export  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssg␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      \`export const loader\` must be a function — non-callable exports crash the SSR runtime with
      \`loader is not a function\`.
    pyreon/missing-get-static-paths  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssg␛[39m  ␛[38;2;250;204;21mwarn␛[39m
      Dynamic route files (\`[id].tsx\`, \`[...slug].tsx\`) should export \`getStaticPaths\` — under
      \`mode: "ssg"\` the SSG plugin silently skips routes without it.
    pyreon/revalidate-not-pure-literal  ␛[38;2;138;134;150mssg␛[39m  ␛[38;2;248;113;113merror␛[39m
      \`export const revalidate = X\` must be a numeric literal or \`false\` — non-literal forms are
      silently dropped from the build-time ISR manifest (PR I limitation)."
`;

